{"agent":"close-brules","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"`rule_inventory` accepts `agent` and then drops it: `RI.inventory(repo)` is called with only the repo. Given `rule_inventory(repo, agent=\"claude\")`, the filter never reaches the census, so the outcome is the full always-loaded inventory rather than that agent's files and byte cost. The parameter is part of the public signature and the stated per-agent inventory, so ignoring it is a wrong result, not an unused import.","digest":"b43f1b28557feb03","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/api/rulesinv.py:11","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/rulesinv.py:11"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"When one path is both a command-dir file and another agent’s rule read, classification and `loaded_by` depend on `HR.load()` order and contradict the “rule glob wins” comment. Instructions are emitted before that harness’s command dir, but a later harness’s `reads` does not repair a row already created as `KIND_COMMAND`: `kind` and `_load_mode` stay `command` / `on request`, so an always-loaded rule (no frontmatter, or `alwaysApply: true`) is omitted from that agent’s `always_bytes`, from `doctor_note` (it drops `KIND_COMMAND`), and from restatement notes. The opposite order hits `continue` and never records the command agent at all, so the census under-states who loads the file.","digest":"5148d85b81adf3e9","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/rulesinv.py:scan_rule_files","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/rulesinv.py:scan_rule_files"}],"chunks_total":4,"coverage":"4/4 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":20845,"diff_sha":"d0a370e63032e8baa7e290c68ac38500f8d05ba13b70524c047bd2f1758df10a","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/B-rules-inventory","diff_stat":{"deletions":16,"files":3,"insertions":37,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":102.3,"excluded_bytes":1608,"excluded_files":1,"excluded_paths":["README.md"],"family":"xai","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"a9f93042f2b5d7d4","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/B-rules-inventory.critic.grok-4.7.20261111T104213Z-bf84dcd4.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4],"reviewed_head":"d4940a6d1410f906e61afe3053b6da5eaab13785","reviewed_paths":{"README.md":"100644 80c329bdfb794c44cc0205fdd9b25d981d979691","ddflow/api/rulesinv.py":"100644 ad222cddbe55a04e62394f1a0065fe108b23deb1","ddflow/services/rulesinv.py":"100644 650928bb7245b8f8394036adee6c583c10f91c6a","ddflow/surfaces/declared/rules.py":"100644 a16f6f5daf3909d7124467874bffe758e36a05e8","tests/test_rules_inventory.py":"100644 81acbed14a894a0849de6993a686ce7b166c558b"},"reviewer":"grok-4.7","reviewer_digest":"1857ec352c55ee94","reviewer_families":["google","xai"],"round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/api/rulesinv.py:11","ddflow/services/rulesinv.py:scan_rule_files"],"tree_sha":"d4940a6d1410+st:575d812c3ae6f2236a4872dc3cf6963f","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"critic","reason":"2 finding(s)"},"id":"eed602e43daa179128382f14f","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":173069,"schema":1,"subject":"B-rules-inventory","ts":"2026-11-11T10:43:55.842566Z"}
